---
description: ML/DL workflow rules (experiments, logging, checkpoints).
globs:
  - "src/train/**/*.py"
  - "src/finetune/**/*.py"
  - "src/evaluate/**/*.py"
  - "configs/**/*.yaml"
---

## Purpose
Run experiments reproducibly with clear configs, logging, and versioned artifacts.

## Applies When
- Files matched by the training/finetune/evaluate/config globs above.

## Do
- Define experiments in YAML: datasets, transforms, hyperparams, schedules, seeds.
- Keep configs immutable at runtime; log any overrides in run metadata.
- Set global seeds; log library versions and environment (CUDA/CPU/RAM).
- Save model, metrics, and exact config per run.
- Track large files with git-lfs or artifact storage.
- Store checkpoints in a versioned hierarchy:
  - `models/v{X}_pipeline/`
  - `models/v{X}_pipeline/v{X}_finetune/`
  - `models/v{X}_pipeline/v{X}_pretrain/`
- Separate train/val/test; report primary metrics and thresholds where relevant.
- Log confusion matrix and PR/ROC when applicable.

## Don’t
- Don’t mutate configs silently during runs.
- Don’t overwrite checkpoints without versioning.

## Commands / Checklist
- Log seeds, env, and resolved config at startup.
- Save `config.yaml`, `metrics.json/csv`, and checkpoints in the run folder.
